'' An EXTERN is a FORWARD DECLARATION, not a definition, so it does not collide with the
'' definition that follows -- nor with a second EXTERN of the same shape.
''
'' The comparison is SYNTACTIC (Collect runs before any type exists) and PERMISSIVE:
'' anything it cannot compare counts as agreeing, because rejecting is the direction that
'' loses a working file. The rejections fbc makes are checked against the corpus, where
'' 29 files exist for exactly that and were passing by accident.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-symbols tests/symbols/src/extern-forward.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' GOLDEN: expected/extern-forward.out
